    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d526">

                <pb facs="0595" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2353/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-21T15:00:00+00:00">January 21, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. My 94, January 18. Military Attaché has discussed this matter with higher
                    military authorities. They have agreed to submit to Salazar<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d526-f1"/> question of juridical status of planes grounded in these
                    circumstances. They have also undertaken to consider a business offer for the
                    purchase of the planes.</p>
                <p>War Department has been informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d526-f1" n="24" xml:id="d526-f1-content">
                <p>Antonio de Oliveira Salazar, President of the Portuguese Council of Ministers and
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
